From 42cb09e39be3f88abd86d9ee65f8e666de317409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(kanban): pin backslash-CR as no line continuation in
 hub-read root stripping [daveey]

Sweep-2039 post-merge check t_01a1d6c5e0bc2fbb found mutant 2559-M8 surviving
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py: widening _CONTINUATION in
hermes_cli/kanban_placement_coordination.py from `\\\n` to `\\\r?\n` (so a
backslash before CR-LF also joins lines) passed all 144 tests.

Bash only drops backslash-LF; a backslash before CR quotes the CR, so
`.\<CR><LF>./x` is no `..`. The new test judges without_read_paths directly:
the CRLF body clears the root path on main and is kept under the mutant; the
LF body is the contrast (a real continuation, kept on both).

Why not a portable_reason row: without_evidence normalises CRLF/CR to LF
before any caller reaches _strip_read_paths, so at that seam the CRLF body
pins on main too (fail-closed) and the mutant is unobservable there. The
row therefore pins the stripper's documented contract.

Proof (hermes-worker-7, base c8246829a6):
- main: 146 passed (144 + 2 new).
- M8 applied: 1 failed,
  test_only_backslash_lf_is_a_continuation[cat ~/.hermes/logs/x.log .\\\r\n./x-True].

Mutant 2559-M7 (dropping the \1 keep) is equivalent: _SPLIT removes every
backslash afterwards. No test added for it.

Card: t_01a1d709fc3c3d42
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py
index aeb828369f..44fe0065e9 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py
@@ -242,6 +242,20 @@ def test_backtick_spans_follow_main_with_or_without_hub_read(attested, body):
     assert reason(body, cfg) == reason(body, cfg, requires=())
 
 
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("body, cleared", [
+    # Only backslash-LF continues a line: a backslash before a CR quotes that CR, so ``.\<CR><LF>.`` is no ``..``
+    # and the root path is cleared (sweep-2039 mutant 2559-M8 read ``\\\r?\n`` as a continuation and kept it).
+    ("cat ~/.hermes/logs/x.log .\\\r\n./x", True),
+    ("cat ~/.hermes/logs/x.log .\\\n./x", False),
+])
+def test_only_backslash_lf_is_a_continuation(attested, body, cleared):
+    # Judged on without_read_paths itself: portable_reason normalises CRLF to LF first (without_evidence), so
+    # there this body pins either way, fail-closed.
+    cfg, _, _ = attested
+    out = coord.without_read_paths(body, cfg, requires=["hub:read"])
+    assert ("~/.hermes/logs/x.log" not in out) is cleared
+
+
 def test_claim_refusal_unchanged(attested):
     _, entry, _ = attested
     card = {"placement_policy": "worker-first-v1", "title": "t", "body": STEP, "requires": ["hub:read"]}
